    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="now" class="doc-h2">Now (2026-11-06)</h2>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Current.</strong> Farm printer id=1, serial
                <code>BECB-D68E-F519-16AB</code>, is linked
                <code>[LAN_HOST:192.168.2.61]</code>. The old address 192.168.2.59
                (and the September address 192.168.2.53) is dead. Staff started a
                print from the queue on 2026-11-06. State at the new address was
                free before that start.</p>
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Operator.</strong>
                Queue <a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/queue') %]" class="doc-link">/3d/queue</a>
                → Start Print. The dialog lists files already on the printer, has a
                search box, and pre-selects a file when the item name and the file
                name share words (Mason Small matches MasonJar_Wide_SmallHole).
                Control remains
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/3d/printer_lan/control') %]?printer_id=1" class="doc-link">/3d/printer_lan/control?printer_id=1</a>.</p>
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Not live until a human restarts :4003.</strong>
                The worker has been up since 2026-11-05 12:16 and does not reload
                <code>.pm</code> files. On disk, a dead address (no route) now
                searches by serial and rewrites <code>[LAN_HOST]</code>. A timeout
                or a refused connection during boot still does not search. Opening
                the queue is meant to start <code>script/printer_lan_sync.pl</code>,
                which enrolls a new Kobra instead of asking staff to attach it.
                None of that runs in the current process. The stored address was
                rewritten by a one-off follow, which is why this print could start.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-body">Tracking:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2334" class="doc-link">todo #2334</a>
                ·
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=206" class="doc-link">project #206 3DPRINT</a>
                · coordinator
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/3dPrintingPlan') %]" class="doc-link">3dPrintingPlan</a>.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="network" class="doc-h2">Network</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Workstation</strong> — dual-home 192.168.1.0 (Ethernet) and 192.168.2.0 (WiFi).</li>
                <li><strong>Production1</strong> — 192.168.1.0 only; OPNsense routes to 192.168.2.0.</li>
                <li><strong>Kobra 3</strong> — WiFi only, 192.168.2.0/24. Proven 2026-11-06 at <strong>192.168.2.61</strong> (port 18910 HTTP, 9883 MQTTS). 192.168.2.59 and 192.168.2.53 no longer answer.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Cloud/app login is not used. LAN Mode on the printer:
            Settings → Network → LAN Mode. Cloud drops while LAN is on.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="protocol" class="doc-h2">Protocol (stock firmware)</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Discover</strong> — TCP :18910 on the chosen subnet (default 192.168.2.1–254), then GET /info. Any open 18910 is a farm candidate.</li>
                <li><strong>Identity</strong> — GET http://HOST:18910/info JSON: modelName, modelId, cn, ctrlType, camera URL, upload URL, token. Not temps or progress.</li>
                <li><strong>Handshake</strong> — signed POST to ctrlInfoUrl with query <code>ts</code> (ms), <code>nonce</code>, <code>sign=md5(md5(token[0:16])+ts+nonce)</code>, <code>did</code>. AES-CBC decrypt <code>data.info</code>. Yields MQTTS broker + username/password. Never log token/password/cert.</li>
                <li><strong>Telemetry / control</strong> — MQTTS :9883, TLS verify off. Subscribe <code>anycubic/anycubicCloud/v1/printer/public/{modelId}/{deviceId}/#</code>. Query types include <code>info</code>, <code>tempature</code> (firmware spelling), <code>print</code>. Pause/resume/stop: type print, action pause|resume|stop, data taskid=-1.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-warning">GET /info is not Moonraker (:7125). Do not invent a preheat-while-idle HTTP command. Stop cancels the job on the machine.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="code" class="doc-h2">Code and URLs</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr><th class="doc-th">Piece</th><th class="doc-th">Where</th></tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Adapter</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>Util::Printing3d::Adapter::Anycubic</code> — sanitize_host, ping, discover, fetch_info, handshake, fetch_state, send_command</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Controller</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>Controller::PrinterLan</code> — do not grow <code>3d.pm</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Farm IP</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Stored as <code>[LAN_HOST:x.x.x.x]</code> in <code>printing_3d_printers.notes</code>. No host column until schema-compare.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Discover</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>/3d/printer_lan/discover?subnet=192.168.2.0/24</code> — attach existing row, do not create a duplicate printer</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Control</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>/3d/printer_lan/control?printer_id=</code> · POST <code>/3d/printer_lan/command</code> cmd=pause|resume|stop</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Templates</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>root/3d/printers.tt</code>, <code>printer_discover.tt</code>, <code>printer_control.tt</code></td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">Changelog fragments:
            <code>2026-09-05-anycubic-discover-compile-fix.inc</code>,
            <code>2026-09-05-kobra3-lan-control.inc</code>.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="next" class="doc-h2">Next session</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li>Human restart of <code>perl script/comserv_server.pl -p 4003 -r</code> so the serial follow, <code>printer_lan_sync.pl</code> enroll, and the stop-requeue / restart-resume behaviour in <code>PrinterLan.pm</code> are actually running. AI does not restart servers.</li>
                <li>Jobs #192 (green top-up, assigned) and #193 (the MasonJar print) are the duplicate pair from before the fix. #193 is the real print. #192 can now be cancelled or completed.</li>
                <li><code>printing_3d_jobs.labour_cost</code> is <code>decimal(10,0)</code> but the result class declares <code>[10, 4]</code>, which is what <code>Manufacturing/Costing.pm</code> and <code>Traveler.pm</code> write (<code>sprintf('%.4f')</code>). Until 2026-11-06 the schema-compare page showed a blank size for every decimal column because <code>ResultParser</code> had no branch for arrayref attributes (<code>size => [10, 4]</code> parsed as undef), so a table sync issued <code>MODIFY col decimal</code> — i.e. back to <code>decimal(10,0)</code>. That is fixed; the page now reads <code>(10,4)</code> and Update Table widens the column correctly. <code>printer_cost</code> and <code>electricity_cost</code> have the same drift (column <code>(10,0)</code>, class <code>(10,2)</code>).</li>
                <li>Start Print pre-selects by shared words, not by an exact file name. Two SmallHole files still tie (1h24m and 1h22m). The printer file record has only a creation timestamp, not last-printed. Last-printed order uses the last 10 completed jobs whose item name contains <code>.gcode</code>.</li>
                <li>Consignment count todo #2666 is paused, not done. Remaining: photo-count section in Documentation/Inventory/consignment, and the decision on pulling stock from another location before printing the shortfall.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="out" class="doc-h2">Out of scope</h2>
